      },
      "dc:source": "communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nauthorised disclosure information means:\n\n(a) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA in\nconnection with the performance of any of the ACMA’s\nfunctions or the exercise of any of its powers; or\n\n(b) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of the\nexercise of any of its powers under:\n\n(i) Part 2, 5, 7 or 13 of the Broadcasting Services Act 1992;\nor\n\n(ii) Chapter 3, 5 or 6 of the Radiocommunications Act 1992;\nor\n\n(iii) Part 3, 6, 21, 26 or 27 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997; or\n\n(iv) Schedule 3A to the Telecommunications Act 1997; or\n\n(v) Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999; or\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nDisclosure by ACMA officials  Part 1\n\nCommunications Legislation Amendment (Information Sharing and Datacasting) Act 2007\nNo. 178, 2007            5\n\n(c) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of the\nexercise of powers under a provision that:\n\n(i) allows the ACMA or an ACMA official to require a\nperson to give information or to produce a document;\nand\n\n(ii) is a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument; and\n\n(iii) is not a provision described in paragraph (b); or\n\n(d) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA by a\ngovernment authority of a foreign country.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\nauthorised disclosure information means:\n\n(a) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA in\nconnection with the performance of any of the ACMA’s\nfunctions or the exercise of any of its powers; or\n\n(b) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of the\nexercise of any of its powers under:\n\n(i) Part 2, 5, 7 or 13 of the Broadcasting Services Act 1992;\nor\n\n(ii) Chapter 3, 5 or 6 of the Radiocommunications Act 1992;\nor\n\n(iii) Part 3, 6, 21, 26 or 27 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997; or\n\n(iv) Schedule 3A to the Telecommunications Act 1997; or\n\n(v) Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999; or\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nDisclosure by ACMA officials  Part 1\n\nCommunications Legislation Amendment (Information Sharing and Datacasting) Act 2007\nNo. 178, 2007            5\n\n(c) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of the\nexercise of powers under a provision that:\n\n(i) allows the ACMA or an ACMA official to require a\nperson to give information or to produce a document;\nand\n\n(ii) is a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument; and\n\n(iii) is not a provision described in paragraph (b); or\n\n(d) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA by a\ngovernment authority of a foreign country.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-2-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7c0177402a1f8cf4bd9156c3b8329136d20b1665dd2574ae2b490b87532e60c4",
      "skos:note": "Definition of authorized disclosure information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007#sch-1-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Section 3",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nauthorised disclosure information means:\n\n(a) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA in\nconnection with the performance of any of the ACMA’s\nfunctions or the exercise of any of its powers; or\n\n(b) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of the\nexercise of any of its powers under:\n\n(i) Part 2, 5, 7 or 13 of the Broadcasting Services Act 1992;\nor\n\n(ii) Chapter 3, 5 or 6 of the Radiocommunications Act 1992;\nor\n\n(iii) Part 3, 6, 21, 26 or 27 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997; or\n\n(iv) Schedule 3A to the Telecommunications Act 1997; or\n\n(v) Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999; or\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nDisclosure by ACMA officials  Part 1\n\nCommunications Legislation Amendment (Information Sharing and Datacasting) Act 2007\nNo. 178, 2007            5\n\n(c) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of the\nexercise of powers under a provision that:\n\n(i) allows the ACMA or an ACMA official to require a\nperson to give information or to produce a document;\nand\n\n(ii) is a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument; and\n\n(iii) is not a provision described in paragraph (b); or\n\n(d) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA by a\ngovernment authority of a foreign country."
    },
