    {
      "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-59c-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to make an instrument a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) Otherwise, an instrument made under subsection (2) is a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "An instrument made under subsection (2) MUST be a legislative instrument."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-59c-ss-4-logic-linearlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "⇒",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If an instrument is not made under subsection (2), then it is NOT a legislative instrument.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) Otherwise, an instrument made under subsection (2) is a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "An instrument made under subsection (2) IS NOT A LEGISLATIVE INSTRUMENT IF IT IS NOT MADE UNDER SUBSECTION (2)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-59c-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "BETWEEN",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The interval between the making of an instrument and its being a legislative instrument is not specified.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) Otherwise, an instrument made under subsection (2) is a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "THE INTERVAL BETWEEN THE MAKING OF AN INSTRUMENT AND ITS BEING A LEGISLATIVE INSTRUMENT IS NOT SPECIFIED."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-59d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59D Disclosure to certain authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007#sch-1-sec-59d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An ACMA official authorised by the Chair, in writing, for the\npurposes of this section may disclose authorised disclosure\ninformation to any of the following authorities if the Chair is\nsatisfied that the information will enable or assist the authority to\nperform or exercise any of its functions or powers:\n\n(a) the Australian Bureau of Statistics;\n\n(b) the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission;\n\n(c) the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority;\n\n(d) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission;\n\n(e) the Commissioner of Taxation;\n\n(f) the Secretary of the Department administered by the Minister\nadministering the Foreign Acquisitions and Takeovers Act\n1975 or an APS employee in that Department whose duties\nrelate to that Act;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nDisclosure by ACMA officials  Part 1\n\nCommunications Legislation Amendment (Information Sharing and Datacasting) Act 2007\nNo. 178, 2007            7\n\n(g) the Secretary of the Department administered by the Minister\nadministering the Classification (Publications, Films and\nComputer Games) Act 1995 or an APS employee in that\nDepartment whose duties relate to that Act;\n\n(h) the Secretary of the Department administered by the Minister\nadministering the Telecommunications (Interception and\nAccess) Act 1979 or an APS employee in that Department\nwhose duties relate to telecommunications or law\nenforcement;\n\n(i) the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(j) the Director of Public Prosecutions;\n\n(k) the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation;\n\n(l) an authority of a State or Territory responsible for enforcing\none or more laws of the State or Territory;\n\n(m) the Regional Telecommunications Independent Review\nCommittee;\n\n(n) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman;\n\n(o) an authority of a foreign country responsible for regulating\nmatters relating to communications or media (including, for\nexample, matters relating to broadcasting or the Internet).\n\n(2) The Chair may, by writing, impose conditions to be complied with\nin relation to authorised disclosure information disclosed under\nsubsection (1).\n\n(3) An instrument made under subsection (2) that imposes conditions\nrelating to one particular disclosure identified in the instrument is\nnot a legislative instrument.\n\n(4) Otherwise, an instrument made under subsection (2) is a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An ACMA official authorised by the Chair, in writing, for the\npurposes of this section may disclose authorised disclosure\ninformation to any of the following authorities if the Chair is\nsatisfied that the information will enable or assist the authority to\nperform or exercise any of its functions or powers:\n\n(a) the Australian Bureau of Statistics;\n\n(b) the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission;\n\n(c) the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority;\n\n(d) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission;\n\n(e) the Commissioner of Taxation;\n\n(f) the Secretary of the Department administered by the Minister\nadministering the Foreign Acquisitions and Takeovers Act\n1975 or an APS employee in that Department whose duties\nrelate to that Act;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nDisclosure by ACMA officials  Part 1\n\nCommunications Legislation Amendment (Information Sharing and Datacasting) Act 2007\nNo. 178, 2007            7\n\n(g) the Secretary of the Department administered by the Minister\nadministering the Classification (Publications, Films and\nComputer Games) Act 1995 or an APS employee in that\nDepartment whose duties relate to that Act;\n\n(h) the Secretary of the Department administered by the Minister\nadministering the Telecommunications (Interception and\nAccess) Act 1979 or an APS employee in that Department\nwhose duties relate to telecommunications or law\nenforcement;\n\n(i) the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(j) the Director of Public Prosecutions;\n\n(k) the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation;\n\n(l) an authority of a State or Territory responsible for enforcing\none or more laws of the State or Territory;\n\n(m) the Regional Telecommunications Independent Review\nCommittee;\n\n(n) the Telecommunications Industry Ombudsman;\n\n(o) an authority of a foreign country responsible for regulating\nmatters relating to communications or media (including, for\nexample, matters relating to broadcasting or the Internet).\n\n(2) The Chair may, by writing, impose conditions to be complied ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-59d-ss-1"
        },
