    {
      "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-59h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59H Disclosure authorised by regulations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007#sch-1-sec-59h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may:\n\n(a) authorise an ACMA official to disclose authorised disclosure\ninformation in specified circumstances; and\n\n(b) provide that the Chair may, by writing, impose conditions to\nbe complied with in relation to the disclosure of authorised\ndisclosure information in those circumstances.\n\n(2) An instrument made under regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(b) that imposes conditions relating to one particular\ndisclosure identified in the instrument is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\n(3) Otherwise, an instrument made under regulations made for the\npurposes of paragraph (1)(b) is a legislative instrument.\n59J  This Part does not limit disclosure by ACMA official\n\nThis Part does not limit the circumstances in which an ACMA\nofficial is authorised to disclose information.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The regulations may:\n\n(a) authorise an ACMA official to disclose authorised disclosure\ninformation in specified circumstances; and\n\n(b) provide that the Chair may, by writing, impose conditions to\nbe complied with in relation to the disclosure of authorised\ndisclosure information in those circumstances.\n\n(2) An instrument made under regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(b) that imposes conditions relating to one particular\ndisclosure identified in the instrument is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\n(3) Otherwise, an instrument made under regulations made for the\npurposes of paragraph (1)(b) is a legislative instrument.\n59J  This Part does not limit disclosure by ACMA official\n\nThis Part does not limit the circumstances in which an ACMA\nofficial is authorised to disclose information.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-59h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-59h-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007-sch-1-sec-59h-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a4181110c9ff5234e1a840b26d2b175419a5ea6484696471fbd03c4ec2d2a295"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/communications-legislation-amendment-information-sharing-and-datacasting-act-2007#sch-1-sec-59h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59H Disclosure authorised by regulations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may:\n\n(a) authorise an ACMA official to disclose authorised disclosure\ninformation in specified circumstances; and\n\n(b) provide that the Chair may, by writing, impose conditions to\nbe complied with in relation to the disclosure of authorised\ndisclosure information in those circumstances.\n\n(2) An instrument made under regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(b) that imposes conditions relating to one particular\ndisclosure identified in the instrument is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\n(3) Otherwise, an instrument made under regulations made for the\npurposes of paragraph (1)(b) is a legislative instrument.\n59J  This Part does not limit disclosure by ACMA official\n\nThis Part does not limit the circumstances in which an ACMA\nofficial is authorised to disclose information."
    },
